  "id": "flat-vector-skyway-hand-reuse-20261015",
  "scope": "Original approved painted pointing gesture reuse on existing Skyway pointer Sprite2D in ignored/nonruntime source controller context. Read authored gesture/source masters/license first; region+rotation+uniform scale only, no bitmap editing/generation/export and no production writes. Verify live tip registration/bob, original targets/callbacks/state and other foreground geometry, whole-hand alpha/readability/hero occlusion and all ten style axes. Record rejected trials, exact source/context hashes and acceptance gaps. Two actually rendered source crop variants are now rejected for standalone wrist/forearm/resolution quality despite original input/bob success. Observer prebinding coordinate metadata is corrected and prior raw readings flagged. Public two-image hand-generation review request remains blocked until explicit destination authorization. Finite20-row caller census is not closure; frozen root registries and production/art/source bytes unchanged. Two-phase payload/final-receipt publication retains all actual per-push gates. Scope refinement before new-art decision: current gesture atlas uses VRAM compression mode2/high_qualityfalse/lossy0.7. Compare original PNG lossless decode in a nonruntime ImageTexture before treating observed softness as a source-resolution failure. Original PNG/import sidecar unchanged; decoding is no pixel repaint or generation. New-art decision deferred pending this safe reuse path. Follow-up completed: originalPNG lossless rendering removes measured import loss but does not fix cut wrist/limited standalone detail; same28px crop new use rejected, sourcePNG loader export warning separate.7runtime cases322checks28cycles plus2source inspections; no original/art/import edits or external export.",
